---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DriveMap from '../../components/DriveMap.astro';
import { DRIVES, driveStats } from '../../lib/trips';

const readout = [
  // Every distance here is the routed one: what the roads actually add up to
  // between the waypoints, not a figure remembered afterwards.
  { label: 'Miles', value: driveStats.roadMiles.toLocaleString() },
  { label: 'Drives', value: String(driveStats.count) },
  { label: 'Coast to coast', value: String(driveStats.crossings) },
];

/** Newest first everywhere else on the site, so newest first here too. */
const ledger = DRIVES;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Driving"
  description="Eight crossings between Seattle and New Hampshire, mapped on real road geometry and weighted by how many times each stretch has been driven."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[88rem]">
    <header>
      <p class="data">
        <a href="/trips" class="hover:text-signal transition-colors">Trips</a>
        <span class="text-rule mx-2">/</span>
        Standing log
      </p>
      <h1 class="font-display mt-5 text-5xl sm:text-7xl">Driving</h1>
    </header>

    <dl
      class="border-rule mt-12 grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-6 border-t pt-6 sm:grid-cols-3"
    >
      {
        readout.map((r) => (
          <div>
            <dt class="data text-graphite">{r.label}</dt>
            <dd class="font-display mt-1 text-2xl tabular-nums">{r.value}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <div class="mt-14">
      <DriveMap />
    </div>

    <section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="ledger-heading">
      <div class="border-rule flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b pb-2">
        <h2 id="ledger-heading" class="font-display text-3xl">The ledger</h2>
        <p class="data">Point at a row to lift that route off the map</p>
      </div>

      {/* Focusable on purpose. The table scrolls sideways on a narrow screen
          rather than pushing the page along with it, and a region that scrolls
          has to be reachable by keyboard or the columns past the edge are only
          available to a pointer. The label is what a screen reader announces
          on arriving in it. */}
      <div class="scroller mt-6" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Drive ledger">
        <table class="log">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" class="data">No</th>
              <th scope="col" class="data">Date</th>
              <th scope="col" class="data">Direction</th>
              <th scope="col" class="data">Route</th>
              <th scope="col" class="data num">Miles</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              ledger.map((drive) => (
                <tr data-drive-row={drive.id} tabindex="0">
                  <td class="data text-signal">{drive.id}</td>
                  <td class="data whitespace-nowrap">{drive.date}</td>
                  <td class="data whitespace-nowrap">
                    {drive.from}
                    <span class="text-rule mx-1">&rarr;</span>
                    {drive.to}
                  </td>
                  <th scope="row" class="route">
                    {drive.route}
                  </th>
                  <td class="num">{drive.roadMiles.toLocaleString()}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="data text-graphite mt-6 max-w-[64ch] leading-relaxed">
        Every distance here is routed rather than remembered: the waypoints are snapped to
        real roads and the mileage is what those roads come to.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="colorado-heading">
      <div class="border-rule border-b pb-2">
        <h2 id="colorado-heading" class="font-display text-3xl">The gully, Colorado, 2024</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy mt-8">
        <p>
          Black Canyon that morning. That evening the bridge over the reservoir was closed and
          the detour ran behind a pilot car, which had made its last run of the night before we
          got there.
        </p>
        <p>
          Backtracking put us on a reservation. We opened their gates and started through, and
          sitting in a gully in full dark the phone went off with a flash flood warning. There
          is no good way to work out how much water is above you or how long you have, and that
          was the part that got to me. We built a path out of rocks to get around a locked gate
          and reached the hotel five hours late.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .scroller {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .log {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .log th,
  .log td {
    border-bottom: var(--rule-width) solid var(--color-rule);
    padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem 0.85rem 0;
    vertical-align: baseline;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .log thead th {
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-graphite);
  }

  .log tbody .route {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    min-width: 22rem;
    max-width: 34rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .log .num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    text-align: right;
    white-space: nowrap;
    padding-right: 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .log thead .num {
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
  }

  .log tbody tr:last-child th,
  .log tbody tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* The row and the route on the map light up together. The tint is shared
     with hover and it is deliberately quiet, which is exactly why the focus
     ring stays: a keyboard user needs to see which row they are on, and a
     tint this faint is not on its own an indicator. The global rule in
     global.css says not to drop the ring without replacing it, and an earlier
     version of this block dropped it. */
  .log tbody tr:hover,
  .log tbody tr:focus-within {
    background: var(--color-paper-sunk);
  }

  .log tbody tr:hover .route,
  .log tbody tr:focus-within .route {
    color: var(--color-signal);
  }
</style>
